# CHANGELOG

## 11-05-26
- Every backup archive now includes a consistent snapshot of the server's own database (settings, services, and backup records), stored at its absolute host path so the future recovery tool and `bsdtar -xpf <archive> -C /` restore it in place
- The host path is found by inspecting the server's own container, a run is reported as partial with the error logged if it cannot be found or the snapshot fails, and a corrupt or missing database is never replaced by an empty one
- All database operations now wait while the snapshot is taken, so nothing is written to the database mid-copy
- The database snapshot appears as `_mediagarrd-server` in each run's service results and in the API's service names
- A service copy of the database file or its `-journal`, `-wal`, and `-shm` files no longer replaces or sits next to the snapshot in the archive
- Documented how to restore the database from an archive

## 10-26-26
- Fixed logic issue with migration versioning
- Added Structurizr diagrams to visualize workflow
- Added Lombok for simpler model classes
- Services are now stored in the database and managed from the `/config` web page or `/api/v1/services`, any service can be backed up
- Backup location can be changed at runtime from `/config` or `PUT /api/v1/config`
- Replaced the per-service runners with a single runner that copies each service's paths through a cached, read-only helper container via the Docker socket
- Added integration test and issue label workflows
- Added first-time web setup reachable from the network, unlocked with a single-use PIN printed in the server logs and disabled once setup is finished
- `docker-compose.example.yml` now works without `install.sh`
- Backup interval and retention count are now stored in the database, retention is settable through `PUT /api/v1/config`, and `GET /api/v1/config` returns every setting
- Configuration changes are rejected while a backup is running so a run never sees its services change underneath it
- Added a pull request check that requires every linked issue to be approved
- Backup archives are laid out by absolute host path with no per-service folder, so they can be restored with `bsdtar -xpf <archive> -C /`
- Archives keep permissions, owners, modification times, symbolic links, and empty directories, and a path that fails to copy no longer leaves partial files in the archive
- Fixed special files (pipes, devices) being archived as empty regular files
- Fixed backup checksums loading the whole archive into memory and dropping leading zeros, and archive sizes over 2 GB being recorded incorrectly
- Every API endpoint now returns errors as `{"error": "..."}` with a matching status code
- The database schema is verified once and then re-checked with a single query per call, rebuilding or upgrading the database whenever it is deleted, altered, or replaced, and moving a corrupt database aside

## 9-23-26
- Add database for keeping records of backups
- Add thorough testing of database functionality
- Add issue templates
- Removed auto-routing to appdata/ within archive to retain actual paths of configs

## 9-16-26
- Adding more detailed logging for service runners
- Renaming QBittorrent's "graveyard" directory to "saved-torrents" to make it less ambiguous

## 9-6-26
- Abstracting services to make adding new ones easier
- Adding new tests
- Project renaming
